            "title": "B. Riley, Booz Allen, Fannie Mae & Freddie Mac: Trending Tickers",
            "description": "<p>Market Catalysts host <a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://www.yahoo.com/author/julie-hyman/?.tsrc=fin-srch\">Julie Hyman</a> tracks several of the day's top trending stock tickers, including B. Riley Financial (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/RILY\">RILY</a>) filing its overdue 10-Q report to the SEC (US Securities and Exchange Commission) to avoid delisting, Booz Allen Hamilton (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/BAH\">BAH</a>) CFO Matt Calderone resigning from the company, and US Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent commenting on his plans for Fannie Mae (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/FNMA\">FNMA</a>) and Freddie Mac (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:5;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/FMCC\">FMCC</a>) IPOs to come in 2026.</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more\u00a0<a data-i13n=\"cpos:6;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/market-catalysts/\">Market Catalysts</a>.</p>",
